# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the SoundFean music application. The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for Vite-based projects.

## Changes Made

### 1. Modified Files
**js/app.js**
- Added import statement: `import { inject } from '@vercel/analytics';`
- Added initialization call: `inject();` at the beginning of the application initialization
- Placed the initialization after all imports and before the main application code runs

### 2. Package Verification
The `@vercel/analytics` package (v2.0.1) was already present in package.json dependencies, so no package.json changes were needed.

## Implementation Details

### Framework-Specific Integration
This project uses **Vite** as its build tool with vanilla JavaScript. According to the official Vercel Analytics documentation, the correct integration method for Vite projects is:

1. Import the `inject` function from `@vercel/analytics`
2. Call `inject()` in the main application entry point

### Location Choice
The analytics initialization was placed in `js/app.js` which is:
- The main entry point of the application (loaded via `<script src="/js/app.js" type="module">` in index.html)
- Executed early in the application lifecycle
- After all module imports but before other initialization code

This ensures that:
- Analytics tracking starts as soon as the application loads
- Page views and user interactions are captured from the beginning
- The integration doesn't interfere with existing functionality (Sentry, Plausible Analytics, etc.)

## Verification

### Build Verification
✅ Build completed successfully with `bun run build`
- No compilation errors
- All chunks generated correctly
- Service worker and PWA files created successfully

### Linting Verification
✅ ESLint passed without introducing new errors
- No new linting errors in js/app.js
- All existing warnings/errors are pre-existing

### Testing
⚠️ Browser tests require Playwright setup and were not run in this environment
- However, the changes are minimal and non-breaking
- Build success indicates no syntax or module resolution issues

## How It Works

Once deployed to Vercel, the analytics will:
1. Automatically track page views
2. Collect Core Web Vitals metrics
3. Monitor user interactions
4. Send data to Vercel's analytics dashboard

### Verification in Production
After deployment, you can verify the integration by:
1. Opening the browser's Network tab
2. Visiting any page on the deployed site
3. Looking for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*` endpoints

## Notes

- The existing Plausible Analytics integration remains intact and will continue to function
- Both analytics systems can run simultaneously without conflicts
- The `inject()` function is lightweight and has minimal performance impact
- No additional configuration is required - analytics will work automatically when deployed to Vercel

## Dependencies

No new dependencies were added. The existing dependency was utilized:
- `@vercel/analytics`: v2.0.1 (already in package.json)

## Compatibility

This implementation is compatible with:
- Vite 7.3.1
- Modern browsers (ES modules support required)
- The existing PWA and service worker setup
- All current integrations (Sentry, Plausible, etc.)
